title: Dashboard › Stage help › What the stages mean
route: /dashboard
intro: The six stage names stay as they are. A closed section at the foot of the Requests card, 'What the stages mean', puts each stage next to the status the rest of Psyflo uses, shows how many requests are in it, and holds the longer note on the progress bars. A stage name in it is also a shortcut to that filter.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Scroll to the foot of the Requests card\nA closed row 'What the stages mean'"
screen sc "Row\nTitle 'What the stages mean'\nOne line: 'Each stage name next to the status Psyflo uses for it, and how many requests are there'"
click c1 "Click the row, or Tab to it and press Enter or Space"
decision d1 "Is it open?"
process p1 "Section opens\nThe chevron turns; the row says it is expanded"
process p2 "Section closes"

group gList "Six lines: stage name, status, count"
  screen l1 "Preparing 5\nDraft while it is being prepared, Ready for review once a person can sign it"
  screen l2 "Received 4\nSubmitted once it is signed and sent, Acknowledged when the payer has it"
  screen l3 "Under review 14\nUnder review"
  screen l4 "Info requested 3\nInfo requested. The payer asked for more information"
  screen l5 "Decided today 8\nApproved or Denied today. Completed once nothing is left to do"
  screen l6 "Appeal or call 8\nDenied, with its route: a call, an appeal, an external review or a resubmission"
endgroup
screen n1 "Note under the list\nThe bars show progress: Prepared, Received, In review, Decided. A denial shows Call, Appeal 1, Appeal 2, External. Over 1.5 × the payer's typical time is late; over 2 × is very late."
process p3 "Counts follow Payer, Program and Request type\nPreparing also counts cases saved in New case that have no row yet"
click c2 "Click a stage name, e.g. 'Under review'"
process p4 "Stage is set to that stage\nAddress gets ?stage=under_review\nThe name is marked pressed"
screen sc2 "Requests\n'Showing 8 of 14' under '14 requests are under review.'"
click c3 "Click the same row again"
end e1 "Section closed again; the filter stays"

goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Key figures › Click a figure to filter the list"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table › Read a row: bars, clock and what happens next"

s1 --> sc --> c1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p1
d1 -->|Yes| p2 --> e1
p1 --> l1 --> l2 --> l3 --> l4 --> l5 --> l6 --> n1
p1 -.-> p3
l1 -.-> c2
c2 --> p4 --> sc2 --> g1
n1 --> c3 --> p2
n1 -.-> g2
